Tornedo makes use of the following open-source projects:

MovieBox-Tui
  https://github.com/mesamirh/MovieBox-Tui
  MIT License. Source of the idea and design reference for Tornedo's
  Watch-online streaming mode (streaming search, Stremio addons, player
  integration, live TV). The streaming architecture, provider probing and
  external-player discovery in Tornedo were modeled on and informed by
  MovieBox-Tui; it is credited here for that inspiration.

Torlink
  https://github.com/baairon/torlink
  MIT License. Used as design and research reference for the federated search
  architecture and several source scraping patterns. Where its code informed
  Tornedo adapters, the logic was re-implemented and adapted; Torlink remains
  credited for its contribution.

WebTorrent
  https://github.com/webtorrent/webtorrent
  MIT License. The torrent engine used behind Tornedo's TorrentClient
  abstraction.

parse-torrent
  https://github.com/webtorrent/parse-torrent
  MIT License. Used for magnet/.torrent parsing.

better-sqlite3
  https://github.com/WiseLibs/better-sqlite3
  MIT License. The SQLite driver for persistence.
